WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.067 --> 00:00:02.100
-That's what I'm talking about.

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.400
Marc Maron.

00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:05.734
Of all the years that
you've been coming here,

00:00:05.734 --> 00:00:07.567
this is the first time
I've ever seen you in a suit.

00:00:07.567 --> 00:00:10.734
-Yeah.
It's -- Well, you know, I --

00:00:10.734 --> 00:00:13.734
when you wear suits, for me --
I don't wear them often.

00:00:13.734 --> 00:00:16.434
All I think about is, like,
don't get food on your suit.

00:00:16.434 --> 00:00:17.701
-Yeah, okay.

00:00:17.701 --> 00:00:18.968
-That's all I'm thinking about.
Right now.

00:00:18.968 --> 00:00:20.000
Is there food?
-No, there's no food.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:20.968
-Okay, good.

00:00:20.968 --> 00:00:21.701
-You have nothing
to worry about.

00:00:21.701 --> 00:00:22.868
You look fantastic.

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:24.167
-I'm surprised
it's not wrinkled, too.

00:00:24.167 --> 00:00:26.267
I'll tell you a story.
-What?

00:00:26.267 --> 00:00:28.167
-So, I get to the airport.
You travel a lot, right?

00:00:28.167 --> 00:00:29.400
-Sure.
-Sure.

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.000
So, all you're thinking about
when you travel,

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.868
is to pack one bag tightly
so you don't have to check it.

00:00:34.868 --> 00:00:35.801
-Of course.
-Right.

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:37.300
That's the key.
Right?

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:39.634
-Yes.
-Now, you fly first, right?

00:00:39.634 --> 00:00:40.734
-Yep.
-Yeah, I fly business.

00:00:40.734 --> 00:00:41.868
I'm not as big as you.
[ Laughter ]

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:44.133
So --
-You tricked me.

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:46.167
You tricked me.

00:00:46.167 --> 00:00:47.367
You tricked me into saying that.

00:00:47.367 --> 00:00:50.033
Yeah, I fly coach.
-Do you?

00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:52.033
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
-Alright.

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:55.868
So, I'm going -- I got my suit
for "The Jimmy Fallon Show,"

00:00:55.868 --> 00:00:56.934
I got my suit.

00:00:56.934 --> 00:00:58.067
And I got my hanging bag.

00:00:58.067 --> 00:00:59.501
Like, I just got the one suit,

00:00:59.501 --> 00:01:01.501
this suit in a bag,
the hanging bag,

00:01:01.501 --> 00:01:04.033
so I can hang it
when I walk in the plane, right?

00:01:04.033 --> 00:01:06.534
Like a business-class guy.

00:01:06.534 --> 00:01:09.901
So, I got my bag, right,
the roller bag.

00:01:09.901 --> 00:01:11.000
I got my carry-on.

00:01:11.000 --> 00:01:12.767
And I got my suit, right?

00:01:12.767 --> 00:01:14.434
So, I'm going to hang it up
in the closet, Jimmy.

00:01:14.434 --> 00:01:15.701
-I know that closet. Yes.

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:18.234
-So, I get to the gate,
and I'm about to go on.

00:01:18.234 --> 00:01:20.501
And the guy goes,
"You got three bags."

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:22.334
I'm like, "No, I don't.
This is a suit.

00:01:22.334 --> 00:01:23.567
It's not a bag."

00:01:23.567 --> 00:01:24.767
He's like, "No, it's three bags,

00:01:24.767 --> 00:01:25.934
so you're going to have
to check something."

00:01:25.934 --> 00:01:27.400
I'm like, "No, I'm not."

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:29.801
[ Laughter ]
-You have to.

00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:31.300
-I'm like, "I'm just going to
put them in the closet."

00:01:31.300 --> 00:01:34.434
He's like, "You can't get
by here with three bags."

00:01:34.434 --> 00:01:37.334
And then, there's a woman --
-He's right.

00:01:37.334 --> 00:01:38.434
-No, he's not.
-Yes.

00:01:38.434 --> 00:01:40.133
[ Laughter ]
-So, there's a woman

00:01:40.133 --> 00:01:42.234
standing there,
and she just looks at me,

00:01:42.234 --> 00:01:44.667
and she goes, "You're going
to have to check a bag."

00:01:44.667 --> 00:01:46.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.501 --> 00:01:48.501
And, like, there's
a line of people behind me.

00:01:48.501 --> 00:01:51.334
And I'm like, "No, I'm not."

00:01:51.334 --> 00:01:52.300
And I'll tell you, folks.

00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:53.501
Folks -- Folks, I'll tell you.

00:01:53.501 --> 00:01:56.267
I opened up my carry-on
and I stuffed my suit...

00:01:56.267 --> 00:01:57.667
[ Laughter ]

00:01:57.667 --> 00:02:02.634
...in that, like,
herky-jerky, angry-old-man way.

00:02:02.634 --> 00:02:04.501
People are watching me,

00:02:04.501 --> 00:02:07.400
but I'm so focused on shoving
my new suit into the bag.

00:02:07.400 --> 00:02:09.634
-How embarrassing.
-I didn't know that.

00:02:09.634 --> 00:02:11.868
All I knew is
that I won somehow.

00:02:11.868 --> 00:02:13.367
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:15.200
[ "Celebration" plays ]

00:02:15.200 --> 00:02:16.601
What happens now?

00:02:16.601 --> 00:02:19.133
-♪ Yahoo! ♪

00:02:19.133 --> 00:02:20.501
-Like, I walked down
that gateway.

00:02:20.501 --> 00:02:22.667
And I'm like, "Yep, I did it."

00:02:22.667 --> 00:02:25.701
As I pulled my wrinkled suit --
-Wrinkled suit, yeah.

00:02:25.701 --> 00:02:26.901
-Small victory, Jim.

00:02:26.901 --> 00:02:27.934
Small victory.

00:02:27.934 --> 00:02:30.200
-You actually look fantastic.

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:31.167
Are you working out?

00:02:31.167 --> 00:02:32.634
Are you healthy?
-Yes, of course.

00:02:32.634 --> 00:02:34.601
You know, I'm dying, Jim.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.601 --> 00:02:36.000
-Wait, what?
-No, I'm just old.

00:02:36.000 --> 00:02:38.400
So, I -- No, I work out.

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:39.601
You know, I work out a lot.

00:02:39.601 --> 00:02:41.634
You know, I actually
just joined a gym.

00:02:41.634 --> 00:02:43.000
It's the first gym I joined
since COVID,

00:02:43.000 --> 00:02:44.300
since, you know, the thing.

00:02:44.300 --> 00:02:45.634
-The pandemic.
-Right.

00:02:45.634 --> 00:02:48.267
So, I was working out outside
on my porch

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:49.801
the whole pandemic
and hiking outside.

00:02:49.801 --> 00:02:52.234
Like, I'm the guy on his
front porch with weights.

00:02:52.234 --> 00:02:54.667
When people walk by, like,
"That's the weight guy."

00:02:54.667 --> 00:02:56.067
[ Laughter ]
-You're that guy.

00:02:56.067 --> 00:02:58.767
-I'm that guy, on the porch
with the weights.

00:02:58.767 --> 00:03:00.067
So, I joined a gym finally.

00:03:00.067 --> 00:03:01.133
It's right down the street
from my house.

00:03:01.133 --> 00:03:02.567
And I joined right in time
for these

00:03:02.567 --> 00:03:04.501
horrendous rainstorms in L.A.,
right?

00:03:04.501 --> 00:03:05.901
It rained for like a week.

00:03:05.901 --> 00:03:07.367
So, I just joined the gym.

00:03:07.367 --> 00:03:10.067
And I went every day, like,
for that week, 'cause I had to.

00:03:10.067 --> 00:03:11.434
I couldn't work out outside.

00:03:11.434 --> 00:03:14.934
So, then the sun comes back out,
and two days,

00:03:14.934 --> 00:03:15.934
I'm enjoying the weather.

00:03:15.934 --> 00:03:17.033
And I get a call on my phone.

00:03:17.033 --> 00:03:18.167
It's a local number.

00:03:18.167 --> 00:03:19.567
So, you've kind of got
to pick it up,

00:03:19.567 --> 00:03:21.434
because maybe there's
an emergency down the street.

00:03:21.434 --> 00:03:24.100
So, I pick up --
I don't know what that means.

00:03:24.100 --> 00:03:26.167
But I pick up the phone --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:26.167 --> 00:03:27.801
I pick up the phone and go,
"Hello?"

00:03:27.801 --> 00:03:29.267
And this guy goes, "Hey, Marc,

00:03:29.267 --> 00:03:31.167
it's John from Equinox
down at the gym.

00:03:31.167 --> 00:03:33.234
You had a pretty good run going.
Just checking in."

00:03:33.234 --> 00:03:35.567
And I had that moment
where I'm like,

00:03:35.567 --> 00:03:37.501
"Is this call coming
from my head?"

00:03:37.501 --> 00:03:41.334
[ Laughter ]
So, I said, "What do you mean?"

00:03:41.334 --> 00:03:42.801
He's like, "Well, you're here
every day.

00:03:42.801 --> 00:03:44.367
Is there anything we can do
to get you back?"

00:03:44.367 --> 00:03:47.501
I'm like, "Dude,
it's been two days."

00:03:47.501 --> 00:03:49.133
Like, what if --
what if I was in trouble?

00:03:49.133 --> 00:03:50.334
What is there, like, "No, man,

00:03:50.334 --> 00:03:52.934
I'm halfway into a sheet cake
over here.

00:03:52.934 --> 00:03:54.367
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.367 --> 00:03:56.567
Yeah, I don't know what
I'm going to do with my life."

00:03:56.567 --> 00:03:57.868
And they're like, "Do you have
a gun in the house?"

00:03:57.868 --> 00:03:59.634
I do, John.
[ Laughter ]

00:03:59.634 --> 00:04:01.133
He's like, "Well,
we'll send someone over.

00:04:01.133 --> 00:04:03.567
Get your shorts on."
[ Laughter ]

00:04:03.567 --> 00:04:06.167
"Can I bring the cake with me?"
"Dude, whatever you got to do."

00:04:06.167 --> 00:04:08.067
[ Laughter ]
-We're here.

00:04:08.067 --> 00:04:11.868
I follow you on the socials,
and you're very entertaining,

00:04:11.868 --> 00:04:14.167
and I saw that you recently got
a new kitten.

00:04:14.167 --> 00:04:15.901
-Yeah, I did --
[ Audience aws ]

00:04:15.901 --> 00:04:17.868
Well, he showed up.

00:04:17.868 --> 00:04:19.334
I don't know what it is.

00:04:19.334 --> 00:04:22.534
I have three cats, and this is
the second one that showed up.

00:04:22.534 --> 00:04:25.934
There was a feral litter outside
of my house, under my house,

00:04:25.934 --> 00:04:28.267
and the mother was moving them
and left this guy.

00:04:28.267 --> 00:04:29.234
[ Audience aws ]

00:04:29.234 --> 00:04:30.701
Yeah, he was like two weeks old.

00:04:30.701 --> 00:04:32.767
And he was this little hairy
ball, and I took him in.

00:04:32.767 --> 00:04:33.834
I don't know what happened to
the rest of them.

00:04:33.834 --> 00:04:34.767
I couldn't save them.
They disappeared.

00:04:34.767 --> 00:04:35.934
But I got this one guy.

00:04:35.934 --> 00:04:37.801
I named him Charlie.

00:04:37.801 --> 00:04:39.701
Charlie Beans Roscoe.

00:04:39.701 --> 00:04:41.467
He's got three names.
Only I know that.

00:04:41.467 --> 00:04:43.234
[ Laughter ]
Only I need to know that.

00:04:43.234 --> 00:04:44.767
-Wow.
-They were all options.

00:04:44.767 --> 00:04:46.534
-No one needs to know that he
has three names.

00:04:46.534 --> 00:04:47.667
-Why would you need to know
that?

00:04:47.667 --> 00:04:49.567
That's Charlie to everyone else,
but to me,

00:04:49.567 --> 00:04:51.067
he's Charlie Beans Roscoe
because...

00:04:51.067 --> 00:04:52.267
[ Laughter ]

00:04:52.267 --> 00:04:53.334
Those were the options.

00:04:53.334 --> 00:04:54.734
I'm like, am I gonna call him
Beans?

00:04:54.734 --> 00:04:56.501
Am I gonna call him Roscoe or am
I gonna call him Charlie?

00:04:56.501 --> 00:04:59.901
So you kind of take a few days,
you're like, "Beans! Nope."

00:04:59.901 --> 00:05:03.133
And then you're like,
"Roscoe, what do you say?"

00:05:03.133 --> 00:05:05.667
Unh-unh. Then you're like,
"Charlie."

00:05:05.667 --> 00:05:07.834
Charlie. Right.

00:05:07.834 --> 00:05:10.834
But I found, you know, having
had three cats,

00:05:10.834 --> 00:05:13.767
that when you have a new kitten,
you spend a lot of time

00:05:13.767 --> 00:05:15.200
saying, "Ow, damn it!"

00:05:15.200 --> 00:05:16.534
[ Laughter ]

00:05:16.534 --> 00:05:19.367
Or like, "Hey, ouch!
What -- God!"

00:05:19.367 --> 00:05:22.167
Or like, "Don't, don't --
Oh, damn it!"

00:05:22.167 --> 00:05:23.300
[ Laughter ]

00:05:23.300 --> 00:05:24.801
-That's what you say when you
have cats.

00:05:24.801 --> 00:05:27.200
-And then you spend a lot of
time trying not to throw a cat.

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:29.200
[ Laughter ]

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:30.834
-You can't throw --
-You know when you pull a kitten

00:05:30.834 --> 00:05:32.534
off something and you have that
moment and you're like,

00:05:32.534 --> 00:05:34.934
"Oh, yeah."
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.934 --> 00:05:37.934
And then you realize, "I could
just drop him kind of hard."

00:05:37.934 --> 00:05:39.701
[ Laughter ]
And then they're like, "Ow!"

00:05:39.701 --> 00:05:41.767
And I'm like, "Yeah, sorry,
a little hard, right?

00:05:41.767 --> 00:05:44.133
Yeah, maybe you don't put
your paw in my food."

00:05:44.133 --> 00:05:45.868
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, my God.

00:05:45.868 --> 00:05:48.067
-Here's the thing about kittens
is, like,

00:05:48.067 --> 00:05:50.267
kittens are great, right?
They're consistent.

00:05:50.267 --> 00:05:51.801
You know, they do
the kitten stuff.

00:05:51.801 --> 00:05:53.734
They're great. It's a great time
to have a cat.

00:05:53.734 --> 00:05:55.567
But you don't know what they're
going to turn into.

00:05:55.567 --> 00:05:57.434
[ Laughter ]

00:05:57.434 --> 00:05:58.767
I had a kitten
a year and a half ago.

00:05:58.767 --> 00:06:01.133
Now he's just this fat sluggo of
a cat.

00:06:01.133 --> 00:06:02.801
[ Laughter ]
Doesn't do anything.

00:06:02.801 --> 00:06:05.334
I don't know if it likes me.
Doesn't like to be touched.

00:06:05.334 --> 00:06:07.200
Always looks confused.

00:06:07.200 --> 00:06:10.100
I have to have him on a special
diet 'cause he's got problems,

00:06:10.100 --> 00:06:12.667
and I'm like, "Now I'm in for
like 17 years of that."

00:06:12.667 --> 00:06:15.601
[ Laughter ]
17 years of people coming over

00:06:15.601 --> 00:06:17.367
and me going, "That's Charlie.
He's awesome.

00:06:17.367 --> 00:06:18.801
That's Buster. He's great.

00:06:18.801 --> 00:06:20.400
Sammy -- I don't know what
happened with this one."

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:22.067
[ Laughter ]
-It's like, "Sammy, hold on.

00:06:22.067 --> 00:06:24.501
It's John from Equinox."
[ Laughter ]

00:06:24.501 --> 00:06:26.834
"Sammy, come back to the club!
Come on, buddy."

00:06:26.834 --> 00:06:29.234
-You can do it, Sammy.
-You can do it, Sammy.

00:06:29.234 --> 00:06:31.567
I want to talk about this --
your stand-up special.

00:06:31.567 --> 00:06:32.534
I'm so excited about this.

00:06:32.534 --> 00:06:34.234
An HBO special.
-Yeah.

00:06:34.234 --> 00:06:35.868
-It means a big deal
for a comedian.

00:06:35.868 --> 00:06:37.334
This is a giant deal.

00:06:37.334 --> 00:06:40.434
[ Cheers and applause ]
Tomorrow night.

00:06:40.434 --> 00:06:42.934
"Marc Maron:
From Bleak to Dark."

00:06:42.934 --> 00:06:44.133
-Yes.

00:06:44.133 --> 00:06:45.300
-It's a fantastic title.

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:46.601
-Isn't it?
-I love it.

00:06:46.601 --> 00:06:48.534
-Listen to me --
-It's perfect.

00:06:48.534 --> 00:06:50.501
It's you.
-It's a real story, dude.

00:06:50.501 --> 00:06:51.634
Like, here's what happened.

00:06:51.634 --> 00:06:53.367
It was kind of funny,
because my buddy,

00:06:53.367 --> 00:06:56.634
Sam Lipsyte, the novelist,
and I sold a show to FX, right?

00:06:56.634 --> 00:06:59.734
So, we wrote a script,
and we delivered it.

00:06:59.734 --> 00:07:01.234
And they were like,
"Great, write another script."

00:07:01.234 --> 00:07:03.167
So, we write another script,
right?

00:07:03.167 --> 00:07:05.968
And we send it to them, right?

00:07:05.968 --> 00:07:07.834
And there's a notes meeting
where they give you notes.

00:07:07.834 --> 00:07:09.534
The network gives you notes,
right?

00:07:09.534 --> 00:07:12.133
So, it's the head of FX,
this guy, Nick Grad,

00:07:12.133 --> 00:07:14.267
and his people and then
my people and me and Sam.

00:07:14.267 --> 00:07:15.667
And we're on a Zoom
call for the notes.

00:07:15.667 --> 00:07:18.267
They're going to tell us
what they think of the script.

00:07:18.267 --> 00:07:20.834
And Nick goes,
"Hey, look, guys, great job.

00:07:20.834 --> 00:07:23.601
Loved it.
Have no specific notes.

00:07:23.601 --> 00:07:26.300
But is there any way we can
get it from bleak to dark?"

00:07:26.300 --> 00:07:27.400
[ Laughter ]

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:30.667
[ "Celebration" plays ]

00:07:30.667 --> 00:07:32.634
-♪ Yahoo! ♪

00:07:32.634 --> 00:07:34.601
[ Laughter ]

00:07:34.601 --> 00:07:36.000
-Marc Maron --
-I did it.

00:07:36.000 --> 00:07:37.334
I nailed it.
-I wanted to show

00:07:37.334 --> 00:07:38.667
everyone a clip.

00:07:38.667 --> 00:07:41.167
Here's a peek at Marc Maron's
"From Bleak to Dark."

00:07:41.167 --> 00:07:43.167
Take a look at this.

00:07:43.167 --> 00:07:45.734
-You think you're a better man
than me

00:07:45.734 --> 00:07:47.501
because you have human kids?

00:07:47.501 --> 00:07:49.868
[ Laughter ]

00:07:49.868 --> 00:07:53.767
Like that makes you
more responsible, more evolved?

00:07:53.767 --> 00:07:55.934
A better human?
Go [bleep] yourself.

00:07:55.934 --> 00:07:58.901
[ Laughter ]
I have three cats that I love.

00:07:58.901 --> 00:08:00.801
And in the best-case scenario,

00:08:00.801 --> 00:08:02.868
I'm going to have to
have them all killed.

00:08:02.868 --> 00:08:08.634
[ Laughter ]

00:08:08.634 --> 00:08:11.501
I'm going to have
to kill my friends.

00:08:11.501 --> 00:08:14.367
And I knew it going in.
That's how big my heart is.

00:08:14.367 --> 00:08:15.567
[ Laughter ]

00:08:15.567 --> 00:08:18.033
-That is so --
that is genius.

00:08:18.033 --> 00:08:19.567
That's a great --
that's so true.

00:08:19.567 --> 00:08:22.767
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:08:22.767 --> 00:08:23.834
I think people are
going to love it.

00:08:23.834 --> 00:08:25.534
I think people
are going to laugh.

00:08:25.534 --> 00:08:27.434
There's also
some emotional stuff

00:08:27.434 --> 00:08:28.534
you talk about in this special

00:08:28.534 --> 00:08:31.200
that really kind of
is moving as well.

00:08:31.200 --> 00:08:33.033
-It gets heavy,
but I balance it.

00:08:33.033 --> 00:08:34.167
You know, there's laughs.

00:08:34.167 --> 00:08:35.300
-It's so cool
that you did it, buddy.

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:36.534
-Yeah.
-It's an amazing show.

00:08:36.534 --> 00:08:38.267
I hope everyone enjoys it.

00:08:38.267 --> 00:08:39.367
You know, every time
you're here --

00:08:39.367 --> 00:08:41.200
thank you again,
for coming on the show --

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:42.667
we talk about music
all the time.

00:08:42.667 --> 00:08:44.567
And we talk about playing
the guitar.

00:08:44.567 --> 00:08:47.267
And we've never actually done
anything crazy with you

00:08:47.267 --> 00:08:48.467
playing the guitar
or something like that.

00:08:48.467 --> 00:08:51.000
But I thought tonight
to celebrate --

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:52.334
No, don't play "Celebrate."

00:08:52.334 --> 00:08:54.968
[ Laughter ]
But to celebrate you being --

00:08:54.968 --> 00:08:57.167
having your own special
on HBO and HBO Max,

00:08:57.167 --> 00:08:58.601
"From Bleak to Dark,"

00:08:58.601 --> 00:09:00.667
would you like to take us into
commercial break with the Roots?

00:09:00.667 --> 00:09:02.467
-Yeah, I'll try. I'll try.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:02.467 --> 00:09:05.501
-Sing with the Roots?

00:09:05.501 --> 00:09:07.667
Go on over, bud.
You got a guitar?

00:09:07.667 --> 00:09:11.701
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:09:11.701 --> 00:09:17.067
♪♪

00:09:17.067 --> 00:09:18.067
-Yeah.

00:09:18.067 --> 00:09:20.434
♪♪

00:09:20.434 --> 00:09:23.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:23.300 --> 00:09:31.934
♪♪

00:09:31.934 --> 00:09:34.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:34.133 --> 00:09:42.167
♪♪

00:09:42.167 --> 00:09:43.334
-What are you talking about?

00:09:43.334 --> 00:09:45.234
Marc Maron right there!

00:09:45.234 --> 00:09:48.067
[ Cheers and applause ]
Dude, you can play.

00:09:48.067 --> 00:09:50.267
"From Bleak to Dark" premieres
tomorrow

00:09:50.267 --> 00:09:52.767
at 10:00 p.m.
on HBO and HBO Max.

00:09:52.767 --> 00:09:54.734
We'll be right back
with more "Tonight Show."

00:09:54.734 --> 00:09:56.634
Stick around, everybody.
Go, dude!

00:09:56.634 --> 00:10:04.300
♪♪

